course: dictionary
lesson: 6036
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and context tells you which one the writer means. «A meltdown is not a tantrum for sweets: it is a brain that has had too much noise and light all at once.» The word tantrum is a clue, so here meltdown means losing control of your feelings, not a nuclear accident.
explain: «Everyone loses control sometimes, especially when overtired; a meltdown is losing control of your feelings, and a simple sorry afterwards usually fixes it.» The sentence explains the meaning for you. Check it by swapping in your meaning: "a moment when someone loses control of their feelings" still makes sense.
explain: «Autism means a brain that works differently; too much noise or light can cause a meltdown, which is not naughtiness.» The writer says a meltdown is not naughtiness, so it is not a choice to misbehave. In a science lesson, meltdown would mean something very different, so always read the words around it.
fact: Meltdown is a noun: a meltdown, meltdowns.
fact: In science, a meltdown is a serious accident in a nuclear power station, when the core gets so hot that it melts.
fact: Informally, a meltdown is a moment when someone loses control of their feelings and cries or shouts.
fact: Informally, a meltdown can also be a sudden total failure or collapse, as in «a market meltdown».
fact: Check which meaning fits by swapping your meaning into the sentence and reading it again.
exercise: «A meltdown is not a tantrum for sweets.» In this sentence, what is a meltdown? | A sudden crash in prices | A serious accident in a nuclear power station | *A moment when someone loses control of their feelings | A quiet sleep after a busy day
exercise: The stock market had a meltdown overnight, and prices crashed. What does meltdown mean here? | A type of toffee | A calm, quiet morning | *A sudden total failure or collapse | A heated argument about dinner
exercise: «Autism means a brain that works differently; too much noise or light can cause a meltdown, which is not naughtiness.» What can cause a meltdown, according to this text? | Going into a nuclear power station | *Too much noise or light all at once | Being told off for being naughty | Being given too many sweets
test: «The reactor core got so hot it nearly had a meltdown.» What does meltdown mean? | Feeling very calm | A type of toffee | A nice cup of tea | *A serious accident when the core melts
test: «After the long day, Sam had a meltdown and shouted at everyone.» What does meltdown mean? | Being very quiet | Winning a race | A holiday in the sun | *Losing control of feelings
exam: Which meaning of meltdown is used in «a market meltdown»? | Overheating in a nuclear reactor | A moment of losing control of feelings | *A sudden total failure or collapse | A small snack
